# Input
```js
/* should generate diagnostics */
import { ref, computed, shallowRef, customRef, toRef, useTemplateRef } from 'vue'
const r = ref(0)
const c = computed(() => r.value)
const sr = shallowRef({ count: 1 })
const cr = customRef((track, trigger) => {
	return {
		get() { return sr.value },
		set(newValue) { sr.value = newValue }
	}
})
const tr = toRef(sr, 'count')
const el = useTemplateRef('el')

console.log(
	r.value,
	c.value,
	sr.value,
	cr.value,
	tr.value,
	el.value,
)

```

# Diagnostics
```
invalid-ref-apis.js:16:2 lint/nursery/noVueRefObjectReactivityLoss ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

  ! This reads the value of a ref only once, so it won't update when the ref changes.
  
    15 │ console.log(
  > 16 │ 	r.value,
       │ 	^^^^^^^
    17 │ 	c.value,
    18 │ 	sr.value,
  
  i This code runs only once, together with the code that creates the ref. The value read here is a copy, and Vue does not update it when the ref changes.
  
  i Read .value inside a function, such as a computed() getter, or pass the ref itself instead of its value.
  
  i This rule belongs to the nursery group, which means it is not yet stable and may change in the future. Visit https://biomejs.dev/linter/#nursery for more information.
  

```

